{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ורבים</b> — The Gaon [Saadia] said: its meaning is, those who awaken shall be for eternal life, and those who do not awaken shall be for reproaches and eternal abhorrence, like והיו דראון (Isaiah 66:24), and the word is one. And the meaning of חרפה is reproach. And the Gaon said: רבים is the few, like ורבים מביאים מנחה (Nehemiah 13:5), and many of the people of the land judaize, and רבים יחלו פני נדיב (Proverbs 19:6). And the reason, in my opinion: the righteous who died in exile shall live when the redeemer comes, for concerning them it is written כימי העץ ימי עמי (Isaiah 65:22), and then they shall enjoy the company of Leviathan and Behemoth and the wild beasts, and die a second time, and live in the resurrection of the dead when they are in the world to come, for they do not eat and drink but only enjoy the radiance of the Shekhinah. And he said: thus is the meaning of ותנוח ותעמוד לגורלך לקץ הימין (Daniel 12:13), in which the book is sealed. And Rabbi Yeshuah said: ישני עפר (Daniel 12:2) is a parable about Israel, who are in exile as though asleep, and behold the redeemer will come for the good of the righteous of Israel and for the harm of their wicked. And the discerning will understand the correct from the two interpretations, and the words of the Sages support the Gaon, of blessed memory."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "I have translated בתים in the phrase כמו בתים as 'asleep' following the root י-ש-ן rather than the more common meaning 'shamed,' as the context of ישני עפר and the parable of exile requires it; the reading is uncertain and the passage may be textually problematic."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:31.480725183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}